From 087b9aab046a2656d226c2a30e77a458ca9c85f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:59:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] survivable processes: review round 2 (scope-only
 shutdown spare, Stop vs every survivable reason, split markers)

- gateway_shutdown spares a persisted job only once it left the unit (detached or its own systemd
  scope), not whenever the key is on: an unscoped persisted job (no usable scope) is killed as today.
- a pending user Stop keeps the tool thread's reason against any survivable reason (backend exit,
  update pause), not only gateway shutdown; the reason set moves to tools/interrupt.py.
- the log reader holds back from the last newline while a session has wrapper markers, so a marker
  trailer straddling two 64 KiB reads is still stripped.
RED (fixes reverted, tests kept): 9 failed; GREEN: 24 passed.
